cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the Remanence software, please cite it as below. The format
  specification DOIs are reserved but not yet published.
title: "Remanence: open tape archival infrastructure and the REM-OBJECT format"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "The ArchiveTech Project"
    website: "https://archivetech.org"
    email: "specs@archivetech.org"
version: 0.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21551570
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/archivetechie/remanence"
url: "https://archivetech.org"
abstract: >-
  Remanence is open Rust infrastructure for writing archives to LTO tape and
  reading them back decades later: library control, tape I/O, erasure-coded
  parity, and a self-describing on-tape object format. The repository is the
  reference implementation of the REM-OBJECT format — a constrained POSIX pax
  tar container with
  per-file SHA-256 identities, closed-form byte-range addressing, a
  deterministic CBOR manifest — its separately versioned REM-ENCRYPT profile,
  and an experimental generation-2 REM-PARITY tape layout for catalog-less,
  parity-protected recovery from bare tape. The generation-1 layout used by
  v0.1.0 is incompatible with this release.
keywords:
  - digital preservation
  - archival storage
  - LTO tape
  - file format
  - erasure coding
  - tar
  - HPKE
